Package: gnome-shell-extension-easyclip
Version: @VERSION@
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: gnome-shell (>= 46), gnome-shell (<< 47~)
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: Brainiac11 <Brainiac11@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Brainiac11/EasyClip
Description: clipboard history and emoji picker for GNOME Shell
 EasyClip opens a small popup on Super+V with everything recently copied,
 text and images alike, plus an emoji picker. Entries can be searched,
 pinned, removed and pasted straight into the focused window.
 .
 The popup takes no input grab: touchpad gestures, workspace switching and
 other shortcuts keep working while it is open.
 .
 After installing, log out and back in, then enable the extension with
 "gnome-extensions enable easyclip@brainiac11.github.io" or from the
 Extensions app.
